    "summary": "On February 6–10, 2017, the James Martin Center for Nonproliferation Studies (CNS) and the African Center for Science and International Security (AFRICSIS) conducted their second joint capacity-building workshop, titled “Nuclear…",
    "body": "<p>On February 6–10, 2017, the James Martin Center for Nonproliferation Studies (CNS) and the <a href=\"https://www.africsis.org/\">African Center for Science and International Security</a> (AFRICSIS) conducted their second joint capacity-building workshop, titled “Nuclear Security Policy and Practice in the African Continent.” AFRICSIS, an independent, science-based non-profit organization established by Mr. Hubert Foy—an alumnus of the <a href=\"http://www.miis.edu/\">Middlebury Institute of International Studies at Monterey</a>—hosted the workshop in Accra, Ghana.</p>"
